From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 09:44:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/57] Changed on disk: the first save never overwrites, also
 with the bar up

A file replaced by rename (temp file + mv) while the tab had unsaved
changes was overwritten by the first Ctrl+S: the watcher had shown the bar
a moment before, and a save while the bar is up counted as Keep mine. Now
the first save only shows the bar; the second save for the same disk
version writes. Repeated watcher events for that version keep the refusal.

The stat cache also keys on the inode: a rename-replace can keep the
modification time and length, and then the cached hash hid the change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/disk_change.rs b/src/disk_change.rs
index ca6b7c9..e3287ff 100644
--- a/src/disk_change.rs
+++ b/src/disk_change.rs
@@ -116,8 +116,25 @@ pub struct DiskWatch {
     pub bar: Option<Bar>,
     /// The disk version the bar was shown for: Keep mine and Save accept this one only.
     shown_for: Fingerprint,
+    /// A save was refused for `shown_for`: the next save writes over it.
+    save_refused: bool,
     /// Modification time, length and hash of the last read, to skip hashing an unchanged file.
-    stat: Option<(SystemTime, u64, u64)>,
+    stat: Option<(Stat, u64)>,
+}
+
+/// What identifies a version of a file without reading it: modification time, length and
+/// inode, as a file replaced by rename can keep the time and length.
+#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]
+struct Stat(SystemTime, u64, u64);
+
+impl Stat {
+    fn of(metadata: &fs::Metadata) -> io::Result<Self> {
+        #[cfg(unix)]
+        let inode = std::os::unix::fs::MetadataExt::ino(metadata);
+        #[cfg(not(unix))]
+        let inode = 0;
+        Ok(Self(metadata.modified()?, metadata.len(), inode))
+    }
 }
 
 impl DiskWatch {
